---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
	title="Tab"
	description="Tab keeps the running tab for your house: who paid, who owes, and what's settled. Free to run yourself, no ads, no limits."
>
	<h1>Tab</h1>
	<p class="lede">Keeps the running tab for your house, so nobody has to.</p>

	<p>
		Housemates, family, a book club, a camping trip: someone always ends up keeping track of who
		paid for what. Tab keeps that record for you. Everyone sees the shared bills, everyone sees
		what they owe, and nobody has to send the "hey, just a reminder" text.
	</p>

	<div class="actions">
		<a class="clay-button" href="/docs/self-host/">Run it yourself</a>
		<a class="clay-button clay-button--soft" href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
	</div>

	<p class="note">
		<strong>Tab is being built in the open.</strong> Version 0.1.0 is the foundation: it runs, but
		you can't log expenses with it yet. Everything below is what it's for.
	</p>

	<h2>What it's for</h2>
	<div class="shelf">
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Splitting bills</h3>
			<p>
				Evenly, by exact amounts, or the real-life way: "$70 off the top for the heater, then 60/40
				for the rest."
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Reading bills for you</h3>
			<p>
				Forward the electric bill's email. Tab suggests the entry and the split; you tap to confirm.
				Nothing is added without you.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Paying back in pieces</h3>
			<p>Pay $40 now and $60 next week. The balance just goes down. No "partially settled" fuss.</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Keeping your spending yours</h3>
			<p>
				Log your own purchases next to the shared ones. Nobody else in the group can see them, not
				even whoever set the group up.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Asking from Claude</h3>
			<p>
				Connect Tab to Claude Code or Claude Desktop and ask "what does Marcus owe me?" It runs on
				your own Claude plan.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Taking your data with you</h3>
			<p>Export everything to a spreadsheet, any time, on every plan.</p>
		</section>
	</div>

	<h2>What it won't do</h2>
	<ul class="plain">
		<li>Show you ads. Not on the free plan, not ever.</li>
		<li>Cap how many expenses you can log a day to push you into paying.</li>
		<li>Sell or share your data.</li>
		<li>Move money. Tab keeps the record; you pay people however you already do.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Two ways to have it</h2>
	<div class="shelf">
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Run it yourself</h3>
			<p>
				Free, forever. One command on a spare computer or a cheap server, and the data never
				leaves your hands. <a href="/docs/self-host/">How to run it</a>
			</p>
		</section>
		<section class="clay-surface">
			<h3>Let us host it</h3>
			<p>
				Not open yet. When it is, every new account gets 3 months of Plus free. After that there's a
				free plan, and Plus, which reads your bills for you, is $10 a year. <a href="/pricing">See pricing</a>
			</p>
		</section>
	</div>
</Page>
